From 0ae4c42f00476577b50e888542fd53270f42eba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Yorkin <vasiliy.yorkin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:51:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: keep agent panes and empty directions on Herdr's
 side

A pane that runs a coding agent is a full-screen application too, so
`direct_keys = "auto"` handed it ctrl+j and ctrl+l, where they mean newline
and nothing at all: pane navigation looked broken in exactly the panes Herdr
is built for. `auto` now forwards to the alternate screen only when no agent
is detected for the pane.

A direct focus chord with no pane in its direction also stops disappearing:
ctrl+l in a pane with no neighbour to the right reaches the shell and clears
the screen, the way it did before those chords were bound.
