 ### Added
-- `keys.direct_keys` and `herdr pane direct-keys` decide who receives prefix-free (direct) keybindings. The values are `herdr` (the default), `auto`, and `pane`. `auto` forwards direct chords to the pane while its application uses the alternate screen, so a full-screen editor keeps its own `ctrl+letter` chords without giving up direct bindings everywhere else. `herdr pane direct-keys` sets the same choice for one pane, and that override lasts as long as the pane does. The per-pane override persists for the life of the pane.
+- `keys.direct_keys` and `herdr pane direct-keys` decide who receives prefix-free (direct) keybindings. The values are `herdr` (the default), `auto`, and `pane`. `auto` forwards direct chords to the pane while its application uses the alternate screen, so a full-screen editor keeps its own `ctrl+letter` chords without giving up direct bindings everywhere else; a pane that runs a detected coding agent is excluded, because those prompts use `ctrl+j` for a newline. A direct focus chord with no pane in its direction reaches the pane instead of being swallowed, so `ctrl+l` still clears the screen. `herdr pane direct-keys` sets the same choice for one pane, and that override lasts as long as the pane does. The per-pane override persists for the life of the pane.
 
